      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "A do kafe?",
      "text": "A at the start turns a sentence into a yes-or-no question: \"A do kafe?\" means \"Do you want coffee?\". Do means \"you want\" and also \"she or he wants\"; dua is \"I want\".",
      "explains": [
        "sq.yes-no-a",
        "sq.dua-object"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "ujë, uji",
      "text": "The same word in two shapes: ujë (water) and uji (the water). Albanian puts \"the\" at the end of the word.",
      "explains": [
        "sq.definite"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 0
    }
  ],
